{"results":[{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P49682","uniProtkbId":"CXCR3_HUMAN","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"C-X-C chemokine receptor type 3"},"shortNames":[{"value":"CXC-R3"},{"value":"CXCR-3"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"CKR-L2"}},{"fullName":{"value":"G protein-coupled receptor 9"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Interferon-inducible protein 10 receptor"},"shortNames":[{"value":"IP-10 receptor"}]}],"cdAntigenNames":[{"value":"CD183"}]},"genes":[{"geneName":{"value":"CXCR3"},"synonyms":[{"value":"GPR9"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12782716"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18174362"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"24469069"}],"value":"Receptor for the C-X-C chemokines CXCL9, CXCL10 and CXCL11, and mediates the proliferation, survival and angiogenic activity of human mesangial cells (HMC) through a heterotrimeric G-protein signaling pathway (PubMed:12782716). Probably promotes cell chemotaxis response. Upon activation by PF4, induces activated T-lymphocyte migration mediated via downstream Ras/extracellular signal-regulated kinase (ERK) signaling"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION","molecule":"Isoform 1"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12782716"}],"value":"Receptor for the C-X-C chemokine CXCL4 and also mediates the inhibitory activities of CXCL9, CXCL10 and CXCL11 on the proliferation, survival and angiogenic activity of human microvascular endothelial cells (HMVEC) through a cAMP-mediated signaling pathway (PubMed:12782716). Does not promote cell chemotaxis response. Interaction with CXCL4 or CXCL10 leads to activation of the p38MAPK pathway and contributes to inhibition of angiogenesis. Overexpression in renal cancer cells down-regulates expression of the anti-apoptotic protein HMOX1 and promotes apoptosis"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION","molecule":"Isoform 2"},{"texts":[{"value":"Mediates the activity of CXCL11"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION","molecule":"Isoform 3"}],"extraAttributes":{"uniParcId":"UPI000004358B"}},
